    "perplexity": {
      "description": "We Are Unpeople is the debut full-length from Unpeople, a twelve-track statement that combines heavy alternative-rock riffs with sharply melodic songwriting. Drawing on grunge, post-hardcore, punk, and modern British alt-rock, the album moves between soaring harmonies, gravelly vocals, swaggering grooves, and explosive bursts of hardcore intensity. Songs such as “Bottle It,” “Haunted,” “The Garden,” and “Swallow” highlight the band’s knack for pairing muscular arrangements with memorable hooks and an energetic, theatrical edge.\n\nReleased through SharpTone, the album presents Unpeople as a young band with both immediate appeal and a distinctive identity, balancing familiar rock influences with inventive dynamics and a strong sense of momentum. Its recurring emphasis on connection and inclusivity gives the record a unifying spirit, while its twelve-song structure maintains a notably consistent pace. This Demon Red vinyl edition adds a striking collector-focused format to an album widely received as an assured and highly promising debut.",
